;; world/rooms/glasswood/x-6y4.room
(room
  region: glasswood
  at: (-6 4)
  title: "Behind the Fall"
  intent: "a hollow behind the frozen curtain that a careful eye finds, where one icicle grows upward and hums a note no stone has"
  bed: (wind 0.0 water 0.2 hum 0.5 drone 0.8)
  light: 0.7
  grid:
  ("#########################"
   "#########################"
   "############      #######"
   "#########           #####"
   "########             ####"
   "#######                  "
   "#######                  "
   "#######                  "
   "#########################"
   "#########################"
   "#########################")
  things: ((upward-icicle at: (13 7)))
  decor: auto)
;; Through the false wall in the Frozen Fall's curtain (its columns 0-3,
;; rows 5-7): a hollow in the rock at the blue hour. THE SECRET (D43): one
;; icicle growing upward from the floor at (13,7), in the middle of the
;; hollow, humming H7's note faintly (the director's upward-hum, the tune
;; tone-h7 when the sound track writes it) and glowing the violet no region
;; uses (the look track's glasswood/upward-icicle@h7). Nothing to take, and
;; the ears never point at it: H7 cannot be found yet.
